#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
nestbox - Nestbox on a Linux host (Ubuntu): the replicas run on this PC.

No sandbox VM in between: this PC is the top row of the table and every
nested replica (appsandbox-replica, a libvirt/KVM guest) is a row under it.
The web UI is the same one the Windows and macOS apps embed (../../../web),
served to the browser on 127.0.0.1 with the same JSON message protocol over
a WebSocket; the replica consoles reach the viewer page through WebSocket
bridges onto their VNC ports, exactly like the WebView2 viewer windows.

    sudo tools/linux/host/nestbox                # installs qemu/libvirt on first run, opens the browser
    sudo tools/linux/host/nestbox --port 8765 --no-browser
    sudo tools/linux/host/nestbox --qemu-patch   # build the identity-patched QEMU for new replicas

Needs root for libvirt and /dev/kvm (the same as appsandbox-replica). Python
3.8+ standard library only.
"""
